1.	Find Get Request in the flow and note the step directly under it.
	2.	Hover over the HRApprovedBy Compose. Click and hold its title bar, then drag it down to the + line directly under Get Request and drop it.
	3.	Do the same with HRApprovalNotes, dropping it under HRApprovedBy.
	4.	Do the same with HRApprovedDate, dropping it under HRApprovalNotes.
	5.	Do the same with the three Comp Composes you added in 4.3 (CompRequestedBy, CompRequestNotes, CompRequestedDate), so all six sit together under Get Request.
	6.	Click Save.

Option 2: if the designer won't let you drag (classic designer)

	1.	On the HRApprovedBy Compose, click ⋯ → Copy to my clipboard.
	2.	Click the + directly under Get Request → Add an action → My clipboard tab → click the copied action. It pastes with the name HRApprovedBy-copy.
	3.	Delete the original HRApprovedBy (⋯ → Delete). Then rename the copy to exactly HRApprovedBy.
	4.	Repeat for HRApprovalNotes and HRApprovedDate.
	5.	Click Save.

Things to watch:

	•	Get Request must stay after the RequestIdText Compose, because its filter uses that. Only the approval Composes move.
	•	The name has to match exactly (no "-copy" at the end). The Token List refers to them as outputs('HRApprovedBy'), outputs('HRApprovalNotes') and outputs('HRApprovedDate').
	•	If Save then shows the same error for a different step (for example the Token List), that step is now above the Composes. Move it below them the same way. Normally it's already further down, so this shouldn't happen.
